#!/bin/sh
# Installs a SimRig update the app downloaded and checked against the release's SHA256SUMS,
# with the system's package tool. The app runs it through pkexec (polkit action
# org.simrig.update), which asks for the password every time.
#
#   simrig-update FILE
#     *.deb             apt-get (resolves dependencies), else dpkg
#     *.rpm             dnf, zypper, else rpm
#     *.pkg.tar.zst     pacman
#     DIR               an extracted release archive: its install.sh
#
# Only SimRig itself: a package with another name is refused.
set -eu
PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
export PATH

src="${1:?usage: $0 FILE}"
case "$src" in
/*) ;;
*) echo "simrig-update: the path must be absolute" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
[ -e "$src" ] || { echo "simrig-update: $src not found" >&2; exit 2; }

# A copy owned by root: the file checked is the file installed. Readable by apt's sandbox user.
work=$(mktemp -d /var/tmp/simrig-update.XXXXXX)
trap 'rm -rf "$work"' EXIT
chmod 0755 "$work"
cp -R "$src" "$work/"
f="$work/$(basename "$src")"
chmod -R a+rX "$f"

not_simrig() {
    echo "simrig-update: $(basename "$src") is not a SimRig package" >&2
    exit 2
}

case "$f" in
*.deb)
    [ "$(dpkg-deb -f "$f" Package)" = simrig ] || not_simrig
    if command -v apt-get >/dev/null; then
        DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y --allow-downgrades "$f"
    else
        dpkg -i "$f"
    fi
    ;;
*.rpm)
    [ "$(rpm -qp --qf '%{NAME}' "$f" 2>/dev/null)" = simrig ] || not_simrig
    if command -v dnf >/dev/null; then
        dnf install -y "$f"
    elif command -v zypper >/dev/null; then
        zypper --non-interactive install --allow-unsigned-rpm "$f"
    else
        rpm -U "$f"
    fi
    ;;
*.pkg.tar.zst)
    pacman -Qip "$f" | grep -Eq '^Name +: simrig$' || not_simrig
    pacman -U --noconfirm "$f"
    ;;
*)
    [ -d "$f" ] && [ -f "$f/install.sh" ] && [ -x "$f/root/usr/bin/simrig" ] || not_simrig
    sh "$f/install.sh" install
    ;;
esac
